  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1234 PM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nSfc high pressure slides to the southeast tonight. That will allow \nweak sfc low pressure to move into central SD. Forcing is pretty \nweak, but there is a marginal risk for severe storms this evening \nwest river. With no marked llj, there's really only a shortwave \nmoving through to get anything going. Could see something develop \nfarther west and maintain itself into Jones/Stanley. \n\nBy Monday afternoon, the weak sfc low slides into eastern SD. The \nmarginal risk shifts with it, stretching from Wheaton, MN to Hayes, \nSD and including points south. Interestingly, ConsShort/ECAM are \npicking up on a few potential storms in the wind gust grids east of \nthe James Valley around 22z. Looks like a couple of bulls-eyes of 35 \nkts. Left them in as the timing seems plausible even if the actual \nlocation may be off a bit. Shortwave activity does pick up between \n21z and 0z and may add enough energy to kick off some storms along \nwith increasing shear. The active pattern extends into Wednesday, \nthough any severe threat will remain south of I-90 on Tuesday. \n\nWhat looks to be a dry and windy cold front moves through on Friday \nwith high pressure building in behind it for next weekend.",
